      "writtenOn": "2022-06-30T16:33:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What about `dp_is entered` to cover the current is_active use?  We\u0027re generally using it as an indication that we\u0027ve entered DP mode and need to still do more stuff to exit.  \n\nThen possibly `dp_is_idle` or `dp_is_inactive` to cover this CL\u0027s use-case.  \n\nI\u0027d half think something like `dp_module_complete` covers the third case.  Though for the third one at least, it seems like it would be more direct for the DP module to notify the DPM when it\u0027s done?",
      "parentUuid": "32fd15d2_8e9adea1",
      "revId": "6eb6de2f9486112d66378fe562a43701204e770f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
